From: cvediver <cvediver@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: force ungraceful MHI teardown on a dead link

With BAR access gated while the link is dead, the graceful MHI power
off starves waiting for device acknowledgements that read back as ~0,
and the recovery wedges after "stopped remote processor q6wcss": WMI
keeps timing out (-108) and the group restart never runs (observed on
the GL-BE9300 bench). The crashed endpoint cannot participate in a
graceful handshake anyway; use the driver's existing FORCE_POWER_OFF
state (mhi_power_down with graceful=false) when the link-dead flag is
set, so teardown completes immediately and power-up's link reset takes
it from there.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
@@ -529,11 +529,13 @@ void ath12k_mhi_stop(struct ath12k_pci *
 	/* During suspend we need to use mhi_power_down_keep_dev()
 	 * workaround, otherwise ath12k_core_resume() will timeout
 	 * during resume.
 	 */
 	if (is_suspend)
 		ath12k_mhi_set_state(ab_pci, ATH12K_MHI_POWER_OFF_KEEP_DEV);
+	else if (test_bit(ATH12K_PCI_FLAG_LINK_DEAD, &ab_pci->flags))
+		ath12k_mhi_set_state(ab_pci, ATH12K_MHI_FORCE_POWER_OFF);
 	else
 		ath12k_mhi_set_state(ab_pci, ATH12K_MHI_POWER_OFF);
 
 	ath12k_mhi_set_state(ab_pci, ATH12K_MHI_DEINIT);
 }
